{
  "case_id": "c22_hour_box_moves_a_receipt_under_500_m",
  "title": "A receipt 510 m away on its own 16-bit box is 490 m away on the hour's 20-bit box and fails",
  "rules": ["lnk_02", "lnk_05"],
  "reasoning": [
    "c22-r sends a 16-bit cell the day before and, at 10:25, the 20-bit cell north-east of that cell's centre, nested inside it. c22-g is one 32-bit fix, stationary. As in c21, c22-r is stationary at all three receipts and the hour's box is r20, which every receipt uses (lnk_02).",
    "The 16-bit centre is the 20-bit cell's south-west corner, so the 20-bit cell holds the 16-bit position's stored value; that position is coarser, not finer, so it sets nothing aside. The 16-bit cell holds the finer 20-bit position and is set aside: the box is r20.",
    "Distance from r20's centre to g32's centre (the fix plus half a unit on each axis): 489.985 m, under 500 m, so every receipt fails lnk_05's per-receipt test with the box it uses (Casey, issue #55, D9).",
    "On their own boxes the receipts at 10:10 and 10:20 would use c22-r's 16-bit cell (c22-m002), 510.009 m from g32, and that cell does not reach g32 (its east edge is about 285 m east of its centre, g32 about 500 m east), so they would pass. The expected result is that they fail.",
    "No receipt is counted, so there is no link-hour."
  ],
